# WI-236 grammar: an id may carry optional per-phase draw weights after
# whitespace — `<ID>[ <PHASE>=<int>]...`, PHASE in BUILD|REVIEW|CRITIQUE|
# DESIGN-CHECK (REVIEW covers both reviewer legs). Unannotated = weight 1
# everywhere (today's behavior); e.g. `OPENAI-TERRA  REVIEW=4` draws OpenAI ~4x
# as often as the weight-1 reviewers. See process-options.md "Unattended
# operation" -> routing for the full rule (0 = fallback-only; malformed = fail).
#
# Contracts: IF-162 — the interface seam this file declares (process.md §8; row
# of record in docs/requirements/interfaces.toml).
#
# Contract IF-162: the enable-list, and the CONSENT surface for managed model
#     selection — routing is on when this file holds at least one entry line and
#     off when it is absent, empty or all comments; one that exists but cannot be
#     read is an error, never routing off. One entry per line in preference
#     order: a registry id, or a version-less token resolved against the model
#     registry to the exact id, else the newest row in its Family-Model line,
#     optionally qualified `@ACCOUNT` by an account table of docs/agents.toml
#     whose cli is the route's (WI-798; unqualified = the person's ambient
#     login); optionally followed by whitespace-separated
#     `<PHASE>=<int>` draw weights over BUILD|REVIEW|CRITIQUE|DESIGN-CHECK, an
#     unannotated entry weighing 1 everywhere. Blank lines and `#` lines are
#     skipped, so this header is not part of the list. An unresolvable token, a
#     malformed annotation and two lines resolving to one id with different
#     weights each fail preflight loudly, naming the offending line — never a
#     silent fall-back to the single-model path.
ANTHROPIC-OPUS-STRONG
OPENAI-SOL
